  "drivers": "Futures are pulling back from Tuesday's record closes for the S&P 500 and Nasdaq Composite: S&P 500 futures −0.4%, Nasdaq-100 −0.7%, Dow −0.8% (about −400 points) and Russell 2000 −0.8%. Oil is the main pressure point — Brent is back above $100 (+1.2% to ~$101.7) and WTI is near $90 after Iran stepped up tanker attacks in the Strait of Hormuz — and Treasury yields are climbing again, with the 10-year at ~5.34% and the 30-year at its highest since 2002 (~5.70%). Chips are leading the decline (SOXX −1.9%, MU −2.5%, AMD −1.9%), crypto is weaker (Bitcoin −3.2%), gold is down 2% and the dollar is firmer. Stock news: Webull −27% on a House panel's China-ties finding, Constellation Brands slipping after reaffirming guidance, and Neogen, Penguin Solutions and Unity (Google AI gaming deal) higher. The September FOMC minutes at 1 p.m. CT and a 10-year note auction at noon CT are the day's main events.",
